Cleanup PR for the gaps surfaced by an audit of the dilf integration
specs (dilf #25 / #26 / #27) against the shipped backend/pedagogy/
implementation. No behaviour change for callers that were already
working; one latent bug fixed.

Schema (spec §10)
- Add idx_move_verdicts_motifs JSON-extract index. The profile
  aggregation query filters by motif name through motifs_json; the
  spec asked for this index up-front but it wasn't there.

API (spec §14.6, plus a real bug)
- Fix missing `await` on explain_verdict in /api/pedagogy/explain-move.
  The function is async in dilf; calling it without await stored a
  coroutine object in the response (the existing tests only covered
  the 404 path so this was never exercised).
- Rebuild the rate-limiter wiring so it actually fires. Now 5/min for
  mode=claude (unchanged target, but no longer a no-op) and 60/min
  for everything else (spec §14.6 courtesy cap). Both limiters reuse
  the existing _make_limiter factory from main.py.

Docs (spec §15)
- New backend/pedagogy/README.md documenting layout, how to add a
  motif detector / template, and the two known gaps for future PRs
  (move-notation parser, distributed rate limiter).

Tests (+6, total 74 green)
- test_fetch_user_games_with_verdicts_orders_desc — verifies the DESC
  ordering promised by storage.py.
- test_explain_move_template_mode_returns_string — regression for the
  await bug above.
- test_explain_move_uses_cache_on_second_call — second hit returns
  cached=true and never re-invokes the explainer.
- test_explain_move_different_lang_creates_separate_cache — fr/en
  rows are stored independently.
- test_get_recommendations_filters_solved — solved exercises are
  excluded from /profile/me/recommendations even when their tag
  matches a profile weakness.
